  "proof": "Each exact eight-wall span is nonsingular and contains a negative direction, so its orthogonal complement is a positive2-plane. In that plane two projected retained walls u,v are independent and have u.v<0. Their positive-definite2x2 Gram matrix has an entrywise strictly positive inverse. For any two nonzero vectors r,s satisfying (r,u),(r,v),(s,u),(s,v)<=0, expressing their pairing via that inverse makes (r,s)>0. Equivalently, the two nonpositive halfplanes meet in a sector of opening strictly smaller than pi/2. Thus no mutually acute-compatible pair of nonzero new normals exists in each of these nine exact planes, with no label bound.",
  "scope": "Only these nine specified orthogonal complements. Does not exclude one cap in a plane, caps in different planes, lower-rank orthogonality, replacement of a retained wall, or different incident spans. The saved strict escape is not asserted to be incident to the nine named walls."
}
